From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: adapt to dma_fence_signal() returning void

Kernel 7.2's dma_fence_signal() (drivers/dma-buf/dma-fence.c) no
longer returns int; it is now `void dma_fence_signal(struct dma_fence
*fence)` and always succeeds internally (the "already signalled" case
is now handled silently inside dma_fence_signal_timestamp_locked()
rather than being surfaced to the caller as an error). Confirmed by
reading both the header declaration and the .c implementation on this
kernel: no error path is returned at all any more.

Both call sites in mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c
(kbase_kcpu_fence_force_signal_process,
kbasep_kcpu_fence_signal_process) captured the old int return value
solely to detect "already signalled" and immediately treat it as
success (`ret = 0`) either way -- i.e. `ret` was always 0 after this
block regardless of branch taken. Since the new API can no longer
report that condition to the caller, the dev_warn() "has been
signalled already" diagnostic is no longer reachable and is removed
along with the dead branch; the call becomes a plain (void) statement
followed by the same unconditional `ret = 0` the old code always
produced. This is a behavior-preserving simplification forced by the
kernel API change, not a functional change: the reachable outcome for
callers of these two functions is identical before and after.

Fixes the mali_kbase.ko build against kernel 7.2.0-rc4-sky1-ncz (next
error after patches 0008-0011 unblocked the devfreq/hrtimer_setup_on_stack/
cix_scmi_register_em/timer_delete translation units).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf_kcpu.c
@@ -1641,12 +1641,8 @@
 	if (WARN_ON(!fence_info->fence))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	ret = dma_fence_signal(fence_info->fence);
-	if (unlikely(ret < 0)) {
-		dev_warn(kctx->kbdev->dev, "dma_fence(%d) has been signalled already\n", ret);
-		/* Treated as a success */
-		ret = 0;
-	}
+	dma_fence_signal(fence_info->fence);
+	ret = 0;
 
 	KBASE_KTRACE_ADD_CSF_KCPU(kctx->kbdev, KCPU_FENCE_SIGNAL, kcpu_queue,
 				  fence_info->fence->context, fence_info->fence->seqno);
@@ -1777,13 +1773,9 @@
 	if (WARN_ON(!fence_info->fence))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	ret = dma_fence_signal(fence_info->fence);
+	dma_fence_signal(fence_info->fence);
 
-	if (unlikely(ret < 0)) {
-		dev_warn(kctx->kbdev->dev, "dma_fence(%d) has been signalled already\n", ret);
-		/* Treated as a success */
-		ret = 0;
-	}
+	ret = 0;
 
 	KBASE_KTRACE_ADD_CSF_KCPU(kctx->kbdev, KCPU_FENCE_SIGNAL, kcpu_queue,
 				  fence_info->fence->context, fence_info->fence->seqno);
